{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":351909,"duration_api_ms":431964,"ttft_ms":4099,"ttft_stream_ms":1159,"time_to_request_ms":135,"num_turns":57,"result":"# Investigation Report\n\n## Task Summary\nThe ticket requests a periodic, constraint-respecting, resumable routine to delete thumbnail/preview cache files whose owning attachment/message record no longer exists. Investigation confirms the codebase already contains every building block needed — an orphan-file diff routine, a resumable-checkpoint job pattern, a daily-cadence alarm-trigger pattern, and the two required job constraints — but none of them are currently composed together with periodicity + resumability + call/battery gating in one place.\n\n## Candidate Cells\n\n| Cell | Reason | Priority |\n|---|---|---|\n| `jobmanager` | Base `Job`, `Job.Parameters`, `JsonJobData` consumed unchanged by the new job. | High |\n| `jobmanager/impl` | `NotInCallConstraint`, `BatteryNotLowConstraint` consumed unchanged. | High |\n| `database` (undocumented `AttachmentTable`) | Existing `deleteAbandonedAttachmentFiles()` / `trimAllAbandonedAttachments()` logic is the algorithmic basis for the new resumable variant. | Medium |\n| `jobs` (ungoverned) | New `Job` subclass lives here, alongside `AnalyzeDatabaseJob` (checkpoint pattern) and `DeleteAbandonedAttachmentsJob` (existing non-periodic orphan cleanup). | Medium |\n| `service` (ungoverned) | New `AlarmListener` lives here, alongside `AnalyzeDatabaseAlarmListener`/`PersistentAlarmManagerListener` (daily-cadence pattern to replicate). | Medium |\n| `keyvalue` (ungoverned, `SignalStore.misc`) | `MiscellaneousValues.kt:288` (`nextDatabaseAnalysisTime`) is the exact precedent for persisting \"next scheduled run\" state. | Low |\n\n## Tracing Summary\n- `AttachmentTable.deleteAbandonedAttachmentFiles()` (`AttachmentTable.kt` ~1775): `context.getDir(\"parts\", MODE_PRIVATE).listFiles()` → filter out `PartFileProtector`-protected files → build `filesInDb` from `SELECT DATA_FILE, THUMBNAIL_FILE FROM attachment` (within `readableDatabase.withinTransaction`) plus `SignalDatabase.stickers.getAllStickerFiles()` → `filesOnDisk - filesInDb` → `File.delete()` each. Single pass, unbounded, no persisted state, no `Job.Parameters` constraints beyond whatever its caller sets.\n- Three callers, verified by grep, none of which need to change: `AttachmentCleanupMigrationJob.java:39` (runs once, at first app run after this feature ships — a migration, explicitly excluded by the ticket as insufficient on its own), `DeleteAbandonedAttachmentsJob.kt:43` (event-driven, `DataRestoreConstraint` only, called from `AppInitialization.java:62` and `ThreadTable.kt:381/412/1381` after specific deletions — bounded scope at call time, so an unbatched full scan is acceptable there), `OptimizeMediaJob.kt:84` (unrelated maintenance job).\n- `AnalyzeDatabaseJob.kt` confirmed: constructor takes `lastCompletedTable: String?`; `serialize()` writes it via `JsonJobData.Builder().putString(...)`; `Factory.create()` reads it back via `JsonJobData.deserialize(data).getStringOrDefault(...)`; `run()` computes `startingIndex` from the checkpoint, processes one table, returns `Result.retry(1.seconds)` if more remain or `Result.success()` when done. `Parameters`: `setMaxInstancesForFactory(1)`, `setLifespan(1.days)`, `setMaxAttempts(UNLIMITED)`. This is the exact resumability shape needed: checkpoint survives process death because `JobManager` persists the job's serialized state to its own store (confirmed via `jobmanager/persistence` cell in schema) and reconstructs it via `Factory` on next run.\n- `AnalyzeDatabaseAlarmListener.kt` confirmed: extends `PersistentAlarmManagerListener` (`service/PersistentAlarmManagerListener.java`), `getNextScheduledExecutionTime()` reads/seeds `SignalStore.misc.nextDatabaseAnalysisTime`, `onAlarm()` enqueues the job then reschedules `getNextTime()` (+1 day, randomized hour/minute) back into `SignalStore.misc`. `schedule(context)` is a static entry point called once from `ApplicationContext.java:544` inside `initializePeriodicTasks()` (confirmed, sits alongside `RotateSignedPreKeyListener.schedule`, `DirectoryRefreshListener.schedule`, etc.). `AndroidManifest.xml:1530-1535` registers it as a non-exported `<receiver>` with a `BOOT_COMPLETED` intent-filter so the alarm chain survives device reboot — this manifest entry is mandatory for any new `AlarmListener`.\n- `MiscellaneousValues.kt:288`: `var nextDatabaseAnalysisTime: Long by longValue(NEXT_DATABASE_ANALYSIS_TIME, 0)` — direct precedent for a new `nextThumbnailCleanupTime`-style property using the same `longValue(...)` delegate.\n\n## Data Flow Analysis\nDisk (`parts` dir file paths) → diffed against DB (`attachment.DATA_FILE`/`THUMBNAIL_FILE` + sticker files) → orphan set → `File.delete()`. For resumability, the new routine must partition this diff into bounded batches and carry a checkpoint (e.g., last-processed file path, mirroring `AnalyzeDatabaseJob`'s `lastCompletedTable`) through `Job.serialize()`/`Factory.create()`, independent of the existing unbatched `deleteAbandonedAttachmentFiles()` used by its three current callers. The periodic trigger's own state (next-run timestamp) flows through `SignalStore.misc`, independent of the job's own batch checkpoint — two separate pieces of persisted state, matching the `AnalyzeDatabaseJob` + `AnalyzeDatabaseAlarmListener` split exactly.\n\n## Manifest Algorithm Analysis\n`jobmanager` CODEMANIFEST's `Job` annotation states: \"Concrete subclasses live outside this cell, throughout the app\" — explicitly anticipates and licenses adding a new subclass without touching this cell's contract. `jobmanager/impl` CODEMANIFEST documents `BatteryNotLowConstraint.isMet()` (\"charging or battery-not-low\") and `NotInCallConstraint` (`isNotInConnectedCall()`, sticky `WebRtcViewModel` EventBus state) exactly as needed — no algorithm change required, only consumption via `Parameters.Builder().addConstraint(KEY)`. Neither cell's CODEMANIFEST documents `AttachmentTable`, so no manifest algorithm exists there to preserve or violate.\n\n## Affected Usages\n| Usage | Cell | Classification | Reason |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| — | `jobmanager` | NOT AFFECTED | No `.usages` files reference job-subclassing or scheduling patterns; cell has no `.usages` directory contents matching this concern. |\n| — | `jobmanager/impl` | NOT AFFECTED | No `.usages` files reference constraint composition. |\n\nNo practices in-scope are directly or indirectly affected — none exist for these concerns.\n\n## Rejected Hypotheses\n- **\"Modify `deleteAbandonedAttachmentFiles()` in place to add batching/resumability.\"** Rejected: it has three live callers (`AttachmentCleanupMigrationJob`, `DeleteAbandonedAttachmentsJob`, `OptimizeMediaJob`) that all currently rely on synchronous, complete-in-one-call semantics (return value `Int` = total deleted, used for logging). Turning it into a multi-call batched operation would change its return-value semantics and force all three callers to adopt new looping/checkpoint-passing logic they don't need — direct violation of Breaking Change Policy question 4 (return value semantics). Rejected in favor of an **additive** batched sibling method reused only by the new job.\n- **\"Reuse `DeleteAbandonedAttachmentsJob` itself, just add constraints + reschedule logic to it.\"** Rejected: its existing callers (`ThreadTable.kt`, `AppInitialization.java`) need immediate, best-effort, bounded-scope cleanup right after a deletion event — adding `NotInCallConstraint`/`BatteryNotLowConstraint` to it would silently defer that event-driven cleanup during a call or low battery, changing its existing observable behavior for existing call sites (Breaking Change Policy question 1). Rejected in favor of a **new, separate** periodic job.\n- **\"Store the batch checkpoint in `SignalStore.misc` instead of the job's own serialized payload.\"** Rejected as sole mechanism: `AnalyzeDatabaseJob` demonstrates the established, in-cell-license pattern is per-job serialized state (survives via `JobManager`'s own persistence, reconstructed through `Factory`); `SignalStore.misc` is reserved in precedent for the *outer* alarm cadence timestamp (`nextDatabaseAnalysisTime`), not per-pass batch progress. Mixing the two would be inconsistent with both precedents it's drawing from.\n\n## Confirmed Root Cause\nNot a defect — a missing composition. All required primitives exist and are independently correct (`deleteAbandonedAttachmentFiles()`'s diff algorithm, `NotInCallConstraint`/`BatteryNotLowConstraint`, the `AnalyzeDatabaseJob` checkpoint-retry pattern, the `AnalyzeDatabaseAlarmListener`/`PersistentAlarmManagerListener` daily-cadence trigger, the `SignalStore.misc` next-run-time precedent). No periodic, resumable, constraint-gated version of the orphan-file cleanup has been assembled from them. Evidence chain: grep-confirmed absence of `NotInCallConstraint`/`BatteryNotLowConstraint` usage anywhere near `DeleteAbandonedAttachmentsJob` or `AttachmentTable`; grep-confirmed `DeleteAbandonedAttachmentsJob` has no `serialize()` payload (`return null`) and no self-retry; grep-confirmed no `AlarmListener` references thumbnail/attachment cleanup.\n\n## Confidence Level\n**HIGH** — every claim above is backed by direct file reads (`AttachmentTable.kt`, `DeleteAbandonedAttachmentsJob.kt`, `AnalyzeDatabaseJob.kt`, `AnalyzeDatabaseAlarmListener.kt`, `PersistentAlarmManagerListener.java`, `MiscellaneousValues.kt`, `AndroidManifest.xml`, `ApplicationContext.java`, both CODEMANIFEST files) plus exhaustive grep for all call sites of the two functions/job being extended, not inference.\n\n## Breaking Change Assessment\n1. Will existing function call with same arguments produce different behavior? **NO** — `deleteAbandonedAttachmentFiles()`, `DeleteAbandonedAttachmentsJob`, and all three of its callers remain untouched; new behavior lives in new, additive code (new method on `AttachmentTable`, new `Job` subclass, new `AlarmListener`, new `SignalStore.misc` property, one new line in `ApplicationContext.initializePeriodicTasks()`, one new `<receiver>` in `AndroidManifest.xml`).\n2. Will existing file paths change? **NO**.\n3. Will output format change? **NO**.\n4. Will return value semantics change? **NO** — no existing signature is altered.\n5. Will manifest-defined guarantees be altered? **NO** — `jobmanager`/`jobmanager/impl` contracts are consumed, not modified; `database` cell's documented types (`SignalDatabase`, `DatabaseTable`, `DatabaseObserver`, `RecipientTable`) are untouched.\n6. Will existing tests break? **NO** — no existing production code path is modified (pending Step 6 confirmation once implementation lands, but by construction of an additive-only plan, no.)\n\nNo breaking change detected. Safe to proceed to Planning.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"6479418a-2b50-46a5-8fc4-0d56e6d55625","total_cost_usd":2.8029931499999994,"usage":{"input_tokens":83,"cache_creation_input_tokens":114017,"cache_read_input_tokens":3351182,"output_tokens":31698,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":114017,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":127,"outputTokens":41561,"cacheReadInputTokens":4085438,"cacheCreationInputTokens":185874,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.8029931499999994,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"e69bc085-b9f8-4cc6-a511-0234792bae3a"}
